From 405abdcc575ceb7e26b21566f8a3728d23a0892a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ayiejosh <132535860+ayiejosh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 14:51:23 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 184/269] gallium/pvr: HWRT sizing, free-list and data-set
 ioctls

The kernel refuses a geometry/fragment job without a hwrt reference, so a render job needs a HWRT data
set, and the data set needs two free lists. Adds the three pieces:

 - pvr_hwrt.c/h: the render-target sizing, ported arithmetically from the working driver
   (pvr_arch_rt_mtile_info_init, pvr_rt_get_tail_ptr_stride_size, pvr_rt_get_isp_region_size). It lives
   in its own translation unit because the hwdef helpers and the generated csbgen headers cannot both be
   included in one file - hwdef makes __pvr_address_type a struct and the csbgen packets then will not
   compile, which is a constraint the driver's own headers already document.
 - pvr_free_list_create() and pvr_hwrt_dataset_create(): the two ioctls.
 - a probe test that computes the sizes and attempts the creation.

Measured on this device: 512x512 -> tiles 32x32, mtiles 4x4, 8x8 tiles per macrotile, TPC 4096 B,
region headers 256 B, simple internal parameter format v2.

Against the real kernel, CREATE_FREE_LIST is refused with EINVAL for a 1..64 page list - the page
counts have to come from the device's free_list_min_pages/free_list_max_pages runtime info, which this
probe path does not query yet. Next step, not a mystery: the same pattern as every other limit in this
driver, where a guessed range is wrong and the kernel says so.

Also reverted my own mess: repeated block insertions had landed test code inside a failure branch twice
and left a duplicate label; pvr_probe.c was restored to its committed state and the block re-applied once.
